# D3 demo, part 1: the runner REACTS to the chaser. About 40 seconds, no training. Run from Examples/AdaptiveTag:
#   Saved/ChaseSim/chase_sim --script Evidence/SAC/d3/demo-reactivity.script
# Each watch uses a simple scripted chaser (greedy = runs straight at the runner; stand = does not move).
# The status line under the board shows the runner's mood: "ignores chaser", "calm" (chaser far) or "FLEEING" (chaser within 40).
# Old runners (square) ignore the chaser. New habit runners (rightturn, clockwise, corner) flee, each in its own habit.
# The dots are the runner's recent trail: watch how it bends when the chaser gets close.

# 1. OLD behaviour: the square runner follows its square no matter what the chaser does.
pattern square
watch 2 60 greedy
# 2. NEW: rightturn. It can only turn right: a gentle right-hand curve while the chaser is far (calm), tighter right turns and loops when it is close.
pattern rightturn
watch 1 60 stand
watch 2 60 greedy
# 3. NEW: clockwise. It goes clockwise round the walls, but swerves inward round the chaser when it gets close.
pattern clockwise
watch 2 60 greedy
# 4. NEW: corner. It sits in a corner until the chaser comes close, then bolts to the corner where it has the biggest lead.
pattern corner
watch 2 60 greedy
# 5. A smarter chaser (intercept: aims where the runner will be) against rightturn, for contrast.
pattern rightturn
watch 1 60 intercept
